Z||000006||West Coast Fiero||12-28-2001||04:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>I prefer <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com/tom" TARGET=_blank>Tom's headlight kits</A>.  I installed mine <I>just</I> before the car went into storage. I have some mods to finish them next spring (including a lexan cover to better keep the Fiero's original hood line).<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tomslights.jpg">  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>is there any visibility problems at night using these that you have encountered?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000007||REDHOTT88||12-28-2001||04:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>I prefer <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com/tom" TARGET=_blank>Tom's headlight kits</A>.  I installed mine <I>just</I> before the car went into storage. I have some mods to finish them next spring (including a lexan cover to better keep the Fiero's original hood line).<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tomslights.jpg">  <P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>HMMMMM... I guess if you want the Mitsubishi 300 look....<P><P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">     <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L V6</B> 5 speed Getrag </FONT><BR>            <I><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, goes fast, red and shiny all over!)</FONT></I>||||reg||9
Z||000008||MinnGreenGT||12-28-2001||04:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR><B> is there any visibility problems at night using these that you have encountered?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I previously had the H4 bulb conversion in the car (and those were very bright in comparison to stock). I was actually a little surprised after I installed them. I have 100w bulbs installed in the kit (normally comes with 50w)- and visibility is fine. Although I would highly recommend replacing the originals with the 100w bulbs... seems like the 50w would be too dim.  The front edge of the hood does block some of light transmission, but it doesn't seem to affect the visibility while driving.<P>So to simplify the answer.  Yes, visibility is still good (but largely due to the brighter bulbs).<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>originally posted by redhot88"<BR><B>HMMMMM... I guess if you want the Mitsubishi 300 look....<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not necessiarly going for the look of copying another car (especially not the 3000GT).  Just a little something different!||||reg||1
