Z||000013||chester||12-28-2001||07:54 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B> Not necessiarly going for the look of copying another car (especially not the 3000GT).  Just a little something different!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>They have a 4 bulb H3 HID conversion that I'm looking to get so I can go with covers and still see.  I have to agree that the 55 watt bulbs are dim.  I have the 100 watt sylvanias but haven't installed them yet. The only drawback to the HID's is price. I would have as much invested in headlights as I paid initially for the whole car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> !!<P><BR>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">        <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension<p>[This message has been edited by chester (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Fierobruiser||12-28-2001||09:26 PM||||I personally like and will get the non pop-up lights and Toms are half the price of RS. I believe that you should be able to do the low pop-up lights by adjusting the headlight stops and then do up a mount so that you could mount the smaller lights. If you got an extra set of headlight units you could even put back in the legal OEM ones for inspection<P>------------------<BR>Notchbacks Rule<BR>85GT(show car)<BR>88Coupe (daily driver)<BR>84 Coupe(project car)||||reg||1
Z||000015||MinnGreenGT||12-29-2001||10:28 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by chester:<BR><B>...The only drawback to the HID's is price. I would have as much invested in headlights as I paid initially for the whole car   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> !!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Agreed! The least expensive HID conversion I've seen is about $600-$800!  WAY too expensive for my budget.  I'll stick with the 100w bulbs for now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
